Description:
  Creates a release from a folder containing application files.  

Usage:
  vpk pack [options]  

Options:
  --outputDir, -o <DIR>              Output directory for created               
                                     packages. [default: Releases]              
  --channel, -c <NAME>               The channel to use for this release.       
                                     [default: win]                             
  --runtime, -r <RID>                The target runtime to build packages       
                                     for.                                       
  --packId, -u <ID> (REQ)            Unique Id for application bundle.          
  --packVersion, -v <VERSION> (REQ)  Current version for application            
                                     bundle.                                    
  --packDir, -p <DIR> (REQ)          Directory containing application           
                                     files for release.                         
  --packAuthors <AUTHORS>            Company name or comma-delimited list       
                                     of authors.                                
  --packTitle <NAME>                 Display/friendly name for                  
                                     application.                               
  --releaseNotes <PATH>              File with markdown-formatted notes         
                                     for this version.                          
  --delta <MODE>                     Disable or set the delta generation        
                                     mode. [default: BestSpeed]                 
  --icon, -i <PATH>                  Path to icon file for package.             
  --mainExe, -e <NAME>               The file name (not path) of the            
                                     main/entry executable.                     
  --exclude <REGEX>                  A regex which excludes matched files       
                                     from the package (in addition to           
                                     built-in defaults). [default:              
                                     .*\.pdb]                                   
  --framework, -f <RUNTIMES>         List of required runtimes to install       
                                     during setup. Example:                     
                                     'net6-x64-desktop,vcredist143-x64'.        
  --splashImage, -s <PATH>           Path to image displayed during             
                                     installation.                              
  --splashProgressColor <COLOR>      Progress bar color (e.g. #FF0000), or      
                                     'None' to hide.                            
  --signTemplate <COMMAND>           Use a custom signing command.              
                                     {{file}} will be substituted.              
  --shortcuts <LOC>                  List of locations to install               
                                     shortcuts to during setup. [default:       
                                     Desktop,StartMenuRoot]                     
  --signParams, -n <PARAMS>          Sign files via signtool.exe using          
                                     these parameters.                          
  --azureTrustedSignFile <PATH>      Path to Azure Trusted Signing              
                                     metadata.json.                             
  --msi                              Compile a .msi machine-wide bootstrap      
                                     package. [default: False]                  
  --msiVersion <VERSION>             Override the product version for the       
                                     generated msi.                             
  --instWelcome <PATH>               Set the plain-text installer package       
                                     welcome content.                           
  --instLicense <PATH>               Set the installer package license          
                                     content. Can be either RTF or              
                                     Markdown.                                  
  --instReadme <PATH>                Set the installer package readme           
                                     content. Can be RTF, Markdown, or          
                                     plain text.                                
  --instConclusion <PATH>            Set the plain-text installer package       
                                     conclusion content.                        
  --instLocation <LOCATION>          Set the installation location.             
                                     [default: Either]                          
  --msiTopBanner <PATH>              Set the top banner strip of the MSI        
                                     dialogs (493x58 BMP).                      
  --msiDialogBackground <PATH>       Set the MSI welcome/finish dialog          
                                     background (493x312 BMP).                  

(*) 7 option(s) were hidden. Use -H / --vhelp to show all options.
